# save: 10-ToThreed
# Sweep segment 10 -> 11: the Twoson hotel phone, the Runaway Five (Yes) and their bus to Threed,
# the cemetery (No Good Fly + Smelly Ghost: Ness PSI Rockin alpha, Paula PSI Fire alpha), the
# gatekeepers' area (flag 46), the Sunset Hotel (the girl, the corridor room: the zombie
# capture), the jail cell door (Paula's prayer), Jeff in Snow Wood (Tony; Maxwell's bent key
# fails on locker npc595, Maxwell's Bad key machine opens it: Pop gun, equipped), the gate
# (Tony's boost), the Winters drugstore (Nancy, Yes: Pak of bubble gum; the Bubble Monkey), the
# terraces south (one Auto Fight battle) to the Lake Tess camp, the cook's stew (night, Jeff
# repairs the spray can), the photographer, Tessie (gum), a Gruff Goat (Big bottle rocket) and
# Brick Road's dungeon door (776,4640). BLOCKED there: Jeff (L3) loses to the dungeon's field
# monsters (Worthless Protoplasm, 17-21 a hit against 35 HP; save 11 has 5 of the 6 beaten at L7) Recorded in chunks with playtest/sweep/rec.py
# late-pads: the port replays the pads the original read after each lag-merged frame
# Doors: skip K / lag (emu frame of K+20) / ignore: idle K+30; idle 14741 is the post-battle
# fade-in. The Sunset Hotel's street door spends 3 more CPU-time frames in the original (the
# emu's LSTEP steps by 2 through the load: lags 17036-17038); the lobby -> corridor fade-in
# ends 4 frames later there (idle 17269-17272)
# The photo's EVENT_450 (absent Ness) and Tessie's riders (EVENT_493/494) copy the BUFFER
# words a failed entity search indexes ($7F0B8C/$7F0BC8, 50c1ad6d): the last map load's
# tileset GFX, which the port now leaves in ert.buffer too (unmasked since then)
